m the DNA cleavage-enhancing drugs etoposide and daunorubicin but not doxorubicin</article-title><source>Clin Cancer Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>3915</fpage><lpage>3924</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Clin Cancer Res||11|3915||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15897593</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kalasz</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biological role of formaldehyde, and cycles related to methylation, demethylation, and formaldehyde production</article-title><source>Mini Rev Med Chem</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>1751</fpage><lpage>1792</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mini Rev Med Chem||3|1751||bib14|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kook</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lepore</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gitler</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Yung</surname><given-names>WWM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mackay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhou</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrari</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruber</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Epstein</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cardiac hypertrophy and histone deacetylase-dependent transcriptional repression mediated by the atypical homeodomain protein Hop</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><year>2003</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>863</fpage><lpage>871</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Invest||112|863||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12975471</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><cit